#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
bell-redteam - BELL-series WiFi PMKID red-team workflow.

Authorized-testing tool for a controlled lab environment. Captures WPA/WPA2
PMKIDs for BELL-series SSIDs, derives candidate passphrases, and cracks them
with hashcat using an evidence-narrowed alphanumeric mask chain.

Official toolchain implemented (hcxtools + hashcat):
    capture    -> wifite --pmkid   (or hcxdumptool directly)
    convert    -> hcxpcapngtool -o <hash>.22000 -E <essid-list>
    filter     -> hcxhashtool -i <all>.22000 -o <bell>.22000 --essid-regex
    candidates -> hcxeiutool (ESSID-derived) + hcxpsktool (weak PSK candidates)
    crack      -> hashcat -m 22000 -a 3 (mask) / -a 0 (wordlist)

Single file, Python 3 standard library only. Runs as a curses TUI by default
and as a non-interactive CLI with subcommands.

References:
  hashcat  hc22000 format, mask attack (-a 3), .hcmask files, mode 22000
  hcxtools hcxdumptool / hcxpcapngtool / hcxhashtool / hcxeiutool / hcxpsktool
  wifite2  --pmkid, --pmkid-timeout, --skip-crack, --hs-dir
  aircrack-ng  airodump-ng, airmon-ng
"""

